[{"id":"8015e6232ed94368aa9e395fc318c351","title":"Gray's atlas city of Lansing, Ingham Co., Michigan","type":"Map Service","url":"https://tiles.arcgis.com/tiles/uHAHKfH1Z5ye1Oe0/arcgis/rest/services/Lansing_1873_Front/MapServer","owner":"wils1301_msugis","description":"<p>1873 map of Lansing ward numbers, streets, railroads, and selected major buildings. Map of Detroit appears on the reverse. This map is a gift of Ronald Dietz.</p><p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>General Disclaimer</strong>:</p><p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>This map was scanned as a 600 dpi TIFF and georeferenced manually using ArcGIS Pro desktop software. Georeferencing was done using 68 GCPs and spline transformation.</p><p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Historic maps are of varying accuracy and meant to be used for general historical comparison. They may not be perfectly geographically accurate but are a perspective of the map authors about the subject contained within. Georeferencing accuracy reflects these considerations.</p><p style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Citation:&nbsp;</strong></p><p style='line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:0em; margin-left:36pt; margin-top:0em; text-indent:-36pt;'><span>Wood, Eugene B., Eugene Robinson , and Ormando Wyllis Gray. “ Gray’s Atlas City of Lansing, Ingham Co., Michigan, 1873 / Compiled by E.B. Wood. Gray’s Atlas City of Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan, 1873 / by Eugene Robinson.” 1:12,000, 1:16,000. Philadelphia, PA: O.W. Gray, 1873. </span><a target='_blank' href='https://catalog.lib.msu.edu/Record/folio.in00003090429' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://catalog.lib.msu.edu/Record/folio.in00003090429</a>.</p>","snippet":"1873 map of Lansing ward numbers, streets, railroads, and selected major buildings.","tags":["Michigan","Lansing"],"access":"public","created":1758722292000,"modified":1759857702000,"typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Map Service","Metadata","Service","WMTS","Hosted Service"]},{"id":"7d784297f7dc4c58bbb550a5ce25c94b","title":"Northwest Neighborhoods CDC","type":"Feature Service","url":"https://services3.arcgis.com/dty2kHktVXHrqO8i/arcgis/